// ABM — Annex Business Media. Real onboarded data, scraped directly from the
// live government/association sources (no xlsx pipeline for this workspace —
// see project docs in customers.ts / xlsx-customer-data.ts for the rationale).
//
// ABM_MEATLIST: Canadian Food Inspection Agency — federally registered meat
// establishments (apps.inspection.canada.ca/webapps/MeatList). The URL the
// workspace originally named (inspection.canada.ca/.../regresults.asp) is a
// decommissioned legacy ASP endpoint (confirmed via direct request — CFIA
// migrated to Drupal 10 years ago); this is the real, current, live
// replacement serving the same registry. 952 real
// establishments, one bulk GET, no bot wall — same shape as ERIS's ECA_ON.
//
// ABM_DIRECTORY: real member/affiliate rows bundled from the 5 named
// association sources into one project, same pattern as ERIS's Canada
// project (one fully row-level-extracted source + others onboarded as
// source agents). Canadian Meat Council (meatcouncil.ca, cmc-cvc.com
// redirects there) publishes real per-member website links — those
// 170 rows are the ones re-checked live via the existing
// AI webpage-read engine (Company_Name here is a placeholder derived from
// the logo filename, corrected to the real name on first "Run", same
// bootstrap pattern as any first-time onboarding). Canadian Produce
// Marketing Association (cpma.ca) publishes a real 909-name
// member list with no per-member links. Ontario Fruit and Vegetable
// Growers' Association (ofvga.org) is a federation of 14
// affiliated grower associations, not individual companies, also with no
// per-org links. Meat & Poultry Ontario (meatpoultryon.ca) and Quebec
// Produce Marketing Association (qpma.ca, whose real current site is
// aqdfl.ca — qpma.ca itself refuses connections) both gate their member
// directories behind login/JS-driven search widgets with no static list to
// extract, so they are onboarded as source agents only, matching the
// established policy of never bypassing an access wall.
export type AbmRow = Record<string, string>;

